From f10e123f837ec9ab891f76fca4cc96ac841a52cf Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: NeoTech <andreas@roughedge.se>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:20:33 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] fix(xtask): pin the env that enters the cargo unit hash for
 gate steps

Cargo 1.100 gives each workspace unit its own directory
target/<profile>/build/<package>/<hash>/, and the hash covers the profile.
Agents ran gates in the shared build worktree with and without
CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0, so each run got a new profile hash and wrote about
600 new camcraft-app units (~190 MB each). Cargo never removes the old ones.

Every cargo call of a gate now gets CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 and loses the
caller's CARGO_PROFILE_* and CARGO_BUILD_INCREMENTAL variables
(xtask/src/unit_env.rs). The gate prints the pin, notes a set RUSTFLAGS,
and its summary prints how many unit directories the run added.

Fixes #3150

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
